  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"770\">\n<li data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"696\">\n<p data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"696\"><span style=\"font-size: 8px;\"><strong data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"578\">Positive staining</strong> indicates the <strong data-start=\"593\" data-end=\"632\">presence of prostatic tissue origin</strong>, most commonly used in identifying <strong data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"695\">prostate adenocarcinoma</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 8px;\" data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"770\">\n<p data-start=\"699\" data-end=\"770\"><span style=\"font-size: 8px;\"><strong data-start=\"699\" data-end=\"720\">Negative staining</strong> suggests <strong data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"754\">non-prostatic origin</strong> of tumor cells.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"805\"><span style=\"font-size: 8px;\"><strong data-start=\"784\" data-end=\"805\">Clinical Utility:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"987\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 8px;\" data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"897\">\n<p data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"897\"><span style=\"font-size: 8px;\">Confirms <strong data-start=\"818\" data-end=\"848\">prostatic origin of tumors</strong>, particularly in <strong data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"896\">metastatic prostate cancer</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 8px;\" data-start=\"898\" data-end=\"987\">\n<p data-start=\"900\" data-end=\"987\"><span style=\"font-size: 8px;\">Useful in differentiating prostate carcinoma from <strong data-start=\"950\" data-end=\"972\">other malignancies</strong> in IHC panels.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
